#
# \brief  Sponge configd persistence scenario — SKELETON (Phase 14 W1)
# \author Sponge OS contributors
# \date   2026
#
# Phase 14 W6 deliverable scenario (docs/plans/phase14-daily-desktop.md
# §W6): boots sponge_configd with <vfs>-activated persistence, drives a
# three-write sequence (panel.height=64, panel.visible_widgets=clock,
# panel.height=28), restarts the daemon, and asserts the broadcast
# carries panel.height=28 after restart (the most-recent value).
#
# This file is a W1-AUTHORED SKELETON only (per the W1 plan, step 3):
# the build list + config + route + gated run_genode_until are in place,
# but the actual configd-persist probe component (the writer/restarter/
# reader) does NOT exist yet. The W6 implementation commit will add
# `test/configd_persist_probe/` to the build list and a start node here,
# then the gated run_genode_until will flip to PASS once the probe emits
# `configd-persist-probe: PASS`.
#
# Until W6 lands, this scenario boots sponge_configd alone and times out
# at the expected sentry (no `configd-persist-probe: PASS` in the log).
# That timeout is the intended FAIL — the scenario proves the build list
# + routing + boot image are sound, and the run tool's run_genode_until
# gate is the W6 acceptance gate.
#
# Topology (skeleton; W6 expands):
#   init
#   + timer
#   + report_rom     (relays config_request / config_result / config
#                     between sponge_configd and the future probe)
#   + sponge_configd (no <vfs> yet — Phase 4 follow-up #2 added the
#                     conditional path; W6 turns the vfs on by default
#                     for the Alpha media with a write-tmp + rename
#                     atomic store write — docs/12 §13.2 contract)
#
# report_rom policies (labels mirror run/sponge-config-probe.run so the
# W6 probe can be added with the same wire contract):
#   sponge_configd's ROM "config_request" <- (probe's "config_request" report)
#   probe's ROM "config_result"           <- sponge_configd's "config_result"
#   probe's ROM "config"                  <- sponge_configd's "config" broadcast
#
# AGENTS.md §4.2 / docs/08-development.md §4.1: this scenario builds
# lib/ld + core init sponge_configd and passes [build_artifacts] to
# build_boot_image so init.xsd + ld.lib.so + the configd binary are all
# staged. Kernel-agnostic in shape (sponge_configd has no Qt6 dep); the
# acceptance run uses KERNEL=sel4 BOARD=pc to match the W1 envelope.
#

build { core lib/ld init timer server/report_rom sponge_configd }

create_boot_directory

install_config {
config
+ parent-provides
  + service LOG
  + service PD
  + service CPU
  + service ROM
  + service IRQ
  + service IO_MEM
  + service IO_PORT

+ default-route
  + any-service
    + parent
    + any-child
+ default | caps: 200 | ram: 8M

+ start timer
  + provides | + service Timer

+ start report_rom | ram: 4M
  + provides
    + service Report
    + service ROM
  + config | verbose: yes
    + policy | label: sponge_configd -> config_request | report: configd_persist_probe -> config_request
    + policy | label: configd_persist_probe -> config_result | report: sponge_configd -> config_result
    + policy | label: configd_persist_probe -> config | report: sponge_configd -> config

+ start sponge_configd | caps: 200 | ram: 16M
  + route
    + service ROM | label_last: config_request | + child report_rom
    + service Report | + child report_rom
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child
- }

build_boot_image [build_artifacts]

#
# Harmless on base-linux (core runs natively); required for base-sel4 /
# QEMU to avoid opening a graphical QEMU window.
#
append qemu_args " -nographic -m 1G "

#
# Verification: the W6 implementation commit will add
# test/configd_persist_probe/ to the build list and a start node here
# (wired to the report_rom policies above), and the probe will:
#   (1) set panel.height=64, panel.visible_widgets=clock, panel.height=28
#       (three writes, via the config_request channel)
#   (2) restart sponge_configd (or re-read the on-disk store from the
#       booted scenario — the exact transport choice is part of W6
#       sub-design, recorded in the W6 commit)
#   (3) read the config broadcast ROM and assert panel.height=28 is
#       present (the most-recent value) — the persistence proof
#   (4) log "configd-persist-probe: PASS"
#
# Until that probe exists, the run_genode_until below times out at the
# PASS marker. That timeout is the EXPECTED FAIL for the W1 skeleton
# and proves the build list + boot image + report_rom routes are sound.
#
run_genode_until {.*configd-persist-probe: PASS.*} 30
